#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262850 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ad0b2008-bd90-5168-be5c-10de1a5ffdf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448260} {:answer/id #uuid "cbfbf81b-2df5-5692-8bdf-b3c476b091e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448261}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448260} :answer-field/id #uuid "93520d72-452c-50c9-97c6-82b2dfb2f65b" :answer-field/key "The coefficient matrix is not invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449170} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91907250-1b71-5208-9c48-56b624cb208a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448262} {:answer/id #uuid "5eb582a7-2819-5150-ac4e-acd82016b49f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448263}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448263} :answer-field/id #uuid "665b8c3b-23dd-500c-a6e4-59240a3ea0f9" :answer-field/key "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is not zero" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449171} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "32d22f54-d568-5c48-a820-4240015e79dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448264} {:answer/id #uuid "07c32ebf-0bc4-563a-88ae-ed188defb588" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448265}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448264} :answer-field/id #uuid "c13fe396-2f57-59c0-b60c-e1db65afd4f0" :answer-field/key "The lines $x+2y=-11$ and $y+7x=4$ intersect at infinitely many  points" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449172}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "012090a8-b5e2-5e56-87ba-9a6b486504ac" :question/math-academy-id "q-127918" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations given by\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-11 \\\\ y+7x &=4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement “The coefficient matrix is not invertible” is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement “The determinant of the coefficient matrix is not zero” is true. According to the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem, the determinant cannot be $0.$\n\n- Statement “The lines $x+2y=-11$ and $y+7x=4$ intersect at infinitely many  points” is false by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The determinant of the coefficient matrix is not zero” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262851 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31393764-2a3b-5f94-a8ad-ec6c335171fd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448266} {:answer/id #uuid "553375c2-cf85-5f9d-bbb0-2230855cf965" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448267}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448267} :answer-field/id #uuid "19c7722a-6979-5033-a8fd-f7b21ac292e9" :answer-field/key "$det(A)\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449173} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a40d55b1-98b2-5ff7-b0b5-62a7b770b2d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448268} {:answer/id #uuid "a5ed1980-c042-5487-b529-f6a360735551" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448269}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448269} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d1d04d4-58b5-55a1-ac37-5e45b973022f" :answer-field/key "$A$ is  invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449174} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61b43c99-11a6-57ed-8a16-f4ef4192ec6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448270} {:answer/id #uuid "71013a10-6913-520b-800b-767fdc89601a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448271}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448270} :answer-field/id #uuid "8901af95-d0b6-584c-8098-fd5186cd5e05" :answer-field/key "$Ax=0$ has a nonzero solution" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449175}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd31265e-20ac-5d02-8e25-ee3bd3fdfd6c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127919" :question/problem "Consider a system of two linear equations in two variables, represented by the matrix equation $Ax=b$ in the usual way. Given that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n1\\. $A$ is invertible.\n\n2\\. The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n3\\. The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n4\\. The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n5\\. $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement $det(A)\\ne 0$ is true by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement “$A$ is  invertible” is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement “$Ax=0$ has a nonzero solution” is false by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statements $det(A)\\ne 0$ and “$A$ is  invertible” are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262852 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193a9a31-72cc-52c6-a705-a7cc0d131106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448272} {:answer/id #uuid "2e608d1e-afec-550f-8c0a-a1b47085d8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448273}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448272} :answer-field/id #uuid "84301b7c-4bac-571e-acbc-02ec8c83029b" :answer-field/key "The lines $2x-2y=-1$ and $3y-x=1$ intersect at infinitely many  points" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449176} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75573dd0-ebb2-5a2b-8aa4-6ff78a5f0d5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448274} {:answer/id #uuid "a7593381-daab-5f1a-a7a3-7c82d8e103ff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448275}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448274} :answer-field/id #uuid "d3bdd369-88e5-5770-a50b-15c5ebdb3612" :answer-field/key "The coefficient matrix is not  invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449177} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54c547b3-1b9f-57e3-be16-35c6dc9d2854" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448276} {:answer/id #uuid "ea577f79-65e8-595e-a0ef-8870c1c707ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448277}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448277} :answer-field/id #uuid "862bba97-dd62-5306-8468-8af85b572b72" :answer-field/key "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is not equal to zero" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449178}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "112c3205-5323-5719-a0c7-431fff65b0ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-127920" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations given by\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-2y &=-1 \\\\ 3y-x &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nGiven that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement “The lines $2x-2y=-1$ and $3y-x=1$ intersect at infinitely many  points” is false by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement “The coefficient matrix is not  invertible” is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement “The determinant of the coefficient matrix is not equal to zero” is true by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statement “The determinant of the coefficient matrix is not equal to zero” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262854 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "69107280-70c4-5ca4-8b64-1e64450165b8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448278} {:answer/id #uuid "4a3f6955-4016-59d3-9db9-3955354a9810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448279}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448279} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ee137d6-1832-58d0-85d5-575e29a0fa26" :answer-field/key "$det(A)\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449179} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29bde20c-189c-54ef-b19c-9e8950c65826" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448280} {:answer/id #uuid "5a9158da-7221-5175-b881-fdd36f8f42ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448281}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448280} :answer-field/id #uuid "de466e8f-4f63-50c6-b72f-38c520f95211" :answer-field/key "$Ax=0$ has no solutions" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449180} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6c45389-9701-5934-b1ac-2f11edac2800" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448282} {:answer/id #uuid "f20f2e0e-7487-58ee-9feb-810b44ca227a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448283}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448283} :answer-field/id #uuid "db9964be-6910-5d74-bd0f-7b3cfcffc16d" :answer-field/key "The lines $x+3y=-1$ and $-x+ky=1$  intersect at exactly one point." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "364a18ef-2de8-57d7-9e2f-631eb4651446" :question/math-academy-id "q-127931" :question/problem "Let $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & k\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix},$ where $k$ is a constant such that $k\\ne -3.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement $det(A)\\ne 0$ is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 3 \\\\ -1 & k\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot k-(-1)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =k+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $k+3\\ne 0$ if $k\\ne -3.$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement “$Ax=0$ has no solutions” is false. According to the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the unique solution to  $Ax=0$ is the trivial one (zero).\n\n- Statement “The lines $x+3y=-1$ and $-x+ky=1$  intersect at exactly one point” is true by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nFinally, only statements $det(A)\\ne 0$ and “The lines $x+3y=-1$ and $-x+ky=1$  intersect at exactly one point” are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262856 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba1c76d6-26c8-504d-9404-70d3044b6d61" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448284} {:answer/id #uuid "52a42a90-a2f2-53a1-a38b-f3fbd471febf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448285}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448285} :answer-field/id #uuid "e1f5a7d6-794e-5b2e-8232-2ef8047378b7" :answer-field/key "$det(A)\\ne 0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3a25b72a-8f61-5c4f-851c-aafa09b763a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448286} {:answer/id #uuid "ecf17fa0-ce5e-57ed-be01-382386d4d6da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448287}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448287} :answer-field/id #uuid "94fe4db0-076c-5d37-abdd-95681679518e" :answer-field/key "$Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2f82e7b-d0c9-554d-b199-c9cd2d9d3e31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448288} {:answer/id #uuid "d21d1cbd-a4f9-59d3-90e9-eebe3afbe948" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448289}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448288} :answer-field/id #uuid "c4af399e-f753-5679-8b6d-af7bd231a29f" :answer-field/key "${A}^{-1}$ does **not** exist" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449184}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "98a38053-dfdc-5995-9d99-1db68e6c6765" :question/math-academy-id "q-127943" :question/problem "Let \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement $det(A)\\ne 0$ is true. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 3-(-1)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement “$Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b$” is true by the second part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement “${A}^{-1}$ does **not** exist” is false. According to the first part of the invertible matrix theorem, the inverse ${A}^{-1}$ must exist.\n\nFinally, only statements $det(A)\\ne 0$ and “$Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b$” are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262876 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4abfb096-6bba-5ea2-bf9c-18957c7e68e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448290} {:answer/id #uuid "5230d7f7-5e35-5729-b0e1-3278e7fe5616" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448291}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448290} :answer-field/id #uuid "8ce3286e-5eb6-554c-b5ea-aa0eacd505cd" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449185} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7e17fb2f-c144-5859-ab19-13769207d987" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448292} {:answer/id #uuid "864b613f-cd1f-51bc-a958-900baa735a20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448293}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448293} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5f91f5f-9b80-5001-94e4-1a6906434452" :answer-field/key "$A$ is invertible" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449186} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7510f705-ade9-5b16-a00a-8c553aa48c7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448294} {:answer/id #uuid "484b7edd-b950-5cae-bafa-4ec7c3c6e9f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448295}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448295} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fafc811-ec3d-58ec-be64-95611287b86a" :answer-field/key "$Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d4f36ed6-3fc6-5f37-801d-3dafa17482c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-128124" :question/problem "Let \n$$\n\\displaystyle A=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$ \nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement $det(A)=0$ is false. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 3-(-3)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =12\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement “$A$ is invertible” is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement “$Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b$” is true by the second part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nFinally, only statements “$A$ is invertible” and “$Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b$” are true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262877 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d364ced3-f0b4-5db0-a418-8e753ca019ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448296} {:answer/id #uuid "c073cf48-e7ec-54b8-aa41-5f5dd4380be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448297}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448296} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fe6ac89-7503-556b-afe3-bc96c1615f30" :answer-field/key "$det(A)=0$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449188} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e79c11e7-6e9c-5e41-a093-0a00d224cc41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448298} {:answer/id #uuid "9f4b969f-164a-59d2-bd0e-77808fa91ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448299}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448299} :answer-field/id #uuid "9fb139ea-e0aa-5492-9328-5084dd32f1a0" :answer-field/key "The system  $Ax=0$ has exactly one solution" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449189} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "151b861f-225f-5d93-94c6-8c117995a350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448300} {:answer/id #uuid "503ffa37-1521-58e6-8ba5-365468b412c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448301}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186448300} :answer-field/id #uuid "262c7598-2a14-5bdc-94d3-bf80698480e8" :answer-field/key "The lines $7x+14y=2$ and $-2x+ky=-3$ intersect at infinitely many points" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449190}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7887fe01-425a-54fe-9f35-ac58c1eba82c" :question/math-academy-id "q-128136" :question/problem "Let $A=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 14 \\\\ -2 & k\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix},$ where $k$ is a constant such that $k\\ne -4.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's now check our statements.\n\n- Statement $det(A)=0$ is false. We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =det\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 14 \\\\ -2 & k\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =7\\cdot k-(-2)\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =7k+28.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that $7k+28\\ne 0$ if $k\\ne -4.$\n\nNow, since the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem is true, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement “The system  $Ax=0$ has exactly one solution” is true. Indeed, by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem, the unique solution to $Ax=0$ is the trivial one (zero).\n\n- Statement “The lines $7x+14y=2$ and $-2x+ky=-3$ intersect at infinitely many points” is false. According to the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem, the lines must intersect at exactly one point.\n\nFinally, only statement “The system  $Ax=0$ has exactly one solution” is true."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cbc51147-25b1-5778-aad6-bf5043f6cb0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463664} {:answer/id #uuid "4313bd7f-c033-58ab-9701-6a606323f354" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463665}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186463664} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb8075aa-0afd-51a1-a5c6-af05a9aed7f2" :answer-field/key "${\\begin{bmatrix}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}$ does not exist" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464766} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "368fae73-e507-5e37-9bef-0792ca0debca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186463666} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b9de64-5f82-5775-b0ce-